    "chunk_text": "3. Policy formulation, projects andprogram implementation inrelation to Tamil mediumschools and state schools as wellas monitoring and evaluating saidschools.\n\n4. Coordinating and supervisingstudent welfare, transport andsanitation of all provincialschools, private schools andinternational schools within aNational Policy Framework.\n\n6. Taking necessary action toimprove education of NationalLanguage and Link Languages.\n\n\u2022 School DevelopmentBoards Act, No. 8 of 1993\n\n\u2022 State Printing CooperationAct, No. 24 of 1968\n\n1. Department of EducationPublications\n\n2. Sri Lanka PublicationDevelopment Bureau\n\n3. National Library andDocumentation Services Board\n\n4. Pirivena Education Board.\n\n5. State Printing Cooperation.\n\nColumn IColumn IIColumn IIIDuties & FunctionsDepartments and StatutoryLaws and OrdinanceInstitutions & Publicto be ImplementedCorporations\n\nSCHEDULE I\n\nState Minister of Education Services\n\nI fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'12'31PART I : SEC. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 31.12.20193A\n\nColumn IColumn IIColumn IIIDuties & FunctionsDepartments, StatutoryLaws and OrdinanceInstitutions & Publicto be ImplementedCorporations\n\nSCHEDULE II (Contd.)\n\nState Minister of Development Banks and Loans\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA.\n\n7. In addition to two MahindaRajapaksha National Schools inHomagama and Matara,commencing 20 modelsecondary schools within firsttwo years as \u201cSuper TrilingualNational School\u201d in the countryso that each district has one suchschool.\n\n8. Ensuring access to education forall children with special needs.\n\n9. Promotion and Development ofSchool Libraries.\n\n10. Student insurance activities as astudent welfare programme.\n\n11. Acting as the mediaspokesperson for the Ministry ofEducation.\n\nPerforming aforementioned duties and functions in coordination with Ministry of Education and relevant institutions.\n\n01 - 454"
